{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "scenario_id": "timestamp_ms_to_us",
  "title": "Timestamp unit changes from milliseconds to microseconds",
  "category": "temporal",
  "description": "A naive timestamp column changes unit from milliseconds to microseconds. Every instant is unchanged. Values include 0001-01-01T00:00:00 and 9999-12-31T23:59:59.999, both outside the range timestamp[ns] can hold, one millisecond before the epoch, and a leap day.",
  "notes": [
    "At the Parquet level the Timestamp logical type's unit changes from MILLIS to MICROS and every stored INT64 is multiplied by 1000.",
    "timestamp[ns] holds 1677-09-21 to 2262-04-11. Combining these two files at nanosecond precision has no nanosecond value for the first two rows."
  ],
